  "caption_latex": "Photon observables for the same local Rabi preparation and weak-end losses as main Fig.~1. {(a):} End-cavity population $\\langle n_1\\rangle$. {(b):} Real nearest-neighbour first-order coherence $10^2\\operatorname{Re}\\langle a_1^\\dagger a_2\\rangle$. {(c):} Real end-cavity first-order coherence $10^2\\operatorname{Re}\\langle a_1^\\dagger a_3\\rangle$. {(d):} Connected end-cavity photon-number correlation $10^3\\langle n_1n_3\\rangle_c$. Every panel compares $J_b/\\omega_c=0,0.1,0.25$ as a function of $\\omega_ct$. Main curves are explicit-cavity references; at $J_b=0.25\\omega_c$, fine dotted lines and shading show independent HOPS means and pointwise 95\\% intervals from physical auxiliary estimators. The zero-hopping cross correlations vanish exactly by factorisation. Photon population alone is not a measure of intersite communication.",
